  "title": "1980 Portuguese presidential election",
  "summary": "The second direct presidential election of the new regime was held on 7 December 1980, three days after Francisco Sá Carneiro died in the Camarate air crash. Ramalho Eanes was re-elected in a single round against General Soares Carneiro, the candidate the Democratic Alliance had put up against him. The date was set by the decree that approved the constitution, which ran the first presidential term to three months after the end of the first legislature. It is in the atlas because the alliance that held the Assembly could not take the presidency with it, and the constitutional revision it carried two years later has to be read against that.",
